  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="f416-ad9a-a457-e804" name="Late Roman (Fall of the West) - List Notes" publicationId="37b4-aae5-6830-d590" hidden="false">
      <description>LATE ROMAN ARMY LIST (Fall of the West, pp.44-48). Percentages are by points. Special rules p.58. Skirmish option, archers mixed into infantry units (one in four) and the Militia standard/musician restriction are rules text only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Roman Army - Limitanei]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Roman Infantry: at least 25%
  Roman Cavalry: up to 60%, at least 20%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Approximately 50% of a Limitanei force by unit would be cavalry (a cavalry unit was half to two-thirds the size of an infantry unit), half light cavalry and half Roman shock cavalry; a heavy shock cavalry unit is very rare. The infantry would not include Palatina but might include Roman veterans and Roman Sagittarii. Special Units only with the opponent's permission.
[Roman Army - Comitatenses]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Roman Infantry: at least 25%
  Roman Cavalry: up to 50%, at least 20%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Approximately one third of a Comitatenses force by unit would be cavalry (smaller units than infantry). Two thirds of the cavalry was Roman shock cavalry; the remainder split between heavy shock cavalry and light cavalry. Special Units only with the opponent's permission. Roman North African armies may be entirely mounted.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
